# ── Reference material (not source) ─────────────────────────
# Full-page screenshots of the live site, kept locally for comparison.
reference ss/

# Scrape + tooling artifacts: scraped WordPress HTML/CSS, generated
# screenshots and throwaway puppeteer scripts (~15MB). Local only.
scratch/

# public/media/ used to be ignored as "generated WebP derivatives", on the
# reasoning that the site served originals from public/images/. That stopped
# being true: src/ now references 25 files under /media/ and only 3 under
# /images/, so the rule was shipping a repo whose every image 404s on a fresh
# clone. The WebPs are the source assets now and belong in the repo (~1MB).

# Frame sources. Vite copies the whole of public/ into dist verbatim, so an
# archive or a source clip left in there ships as megabytes nothing ever
# requests - the ones behind this sequence now live in assets-src/sequence/
# instead, and these rules guard against the next one landing in the web root.
public/**/*.zip
public/*.mp4

# The archive itself is not tracked: its 240 frames are, under
# public/sequence/, which is what the site actually serves. Keeping both
# would put the same 1.2MB in the repo twice.
assets-src/sequence/*.zip
assets-src/sequence/*.mp4
BACKEND-PLAN.md
fornt-design-.md